            <title>[LU-20272] NULL deref of out_clean_llog_fileset in nodemap_del()</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20272</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In nodemap_del() around line 4364, there's this check:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (fileset_prim_exists &amp;amp;&amp;amp; !rc &amp;amp;&amp;amp; !nodemap-&amp;gt;nmf_fileset_use_iam &amp;amp;&amp;amp;
  !nodemap-&amp;gt;nm_dyn)
  *out_clean_llog_fileset = &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But nodemap_del() is called with NULL for that param at line 4311 (nodemap_del(nm-&amp;gt;nm_name, NULL)). The other two spots in the same function do guard with &amp;amp;&amp;amp; out_clean_llog_fileset before dereferencing, so it looks like this one just got missed?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Discovered by code inspect.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
